# TrafIQ — production build config, loaded automatically by Vite for
# `vite build` (mode "production"). Committed on purpose.
#
# WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
# `.env.local` is gitignored and is therefore NOT uploaded to a host, so a
# deploy on Vercel/Render/Netlify built without these values and silently fell
# back to local demo mode — the "Firebase / Data: Demo store" status.
# Committing them here means any production build is configured out of the box.
#
# IS THIS SAFE TO COMMIT?
# Yes. These are Firebase **Web SDK client identifiers**, not credentials.
# Google publishes them in the browser bundle by design. Access is controlled by
# `firestore.rules` (+ API key restrictions in Google Cloud), never by hiding
# these values. Never put a service-account JSON or Admin SDK key here.
#
# Values come from Firebase Console -> Project settings -> Your apps.
#
# NOTE: Vite gives `.env.local` priority over this file, so local development
# still uses `.env.local`. To override these on a host instead, set the same
# VITE_FIREBASE_* names in the host's environment-variable settings.

VITE_FIREBASE_API_KEY="AIzaSyByyL0MS2DAUzJBNeOTEStQOmsB8XZO8M4"
VITE_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN="trafiq-7680f.firebaseapp.com"
VITE_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID="trafiq-7680f"
VITE_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET="trafiq-7680f.firebasestorage.app"
VITE_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID="512367291994"
VITE_FIREBASE_APP_ID="1:512367291994:web:ee05cdcd954eb2c9abb263"
